---
title: Local Development
description: Run Lament locally for development and testing.
section: Getting Started
order: 2
---

## Running the API

The API server uses Hono with `tsx` for development:

```bash
cd lament-api
bun run dev
```

This starts the API at `http://localhost:3000` using `tsx --watch` for hot reloading.

For the edge-compatible version (Cloudflare Workers), use `wrangler`:

```bash
bunx wrangler dev
```

## Running the Frontend

The SvelteKit frontend connects to the API through server-side proxy endpoints:

```bash
cd lament
bun run dev
```

The frontend dev server starts at `http://localhost:5173`.

## Running the Docs

```bash
cd lament-docs
bun run dev
```

The documentation site starts at `http://localhost:5174` (or next available port).

## Running the Scraper

The scraper is a CLI tool, not a server. Run individual commands:

```bash
cd lament-scrapper
bun run dev
```

See [Scraper Architecture](/docs/scraper/architecture) for details on scraper commands.

## Full Stack Development

To run the full stack locally, start the API and frontend in separate terminals:

**Terminal 1 — API:**
```bash
cd lament-api && bun run dev
```

**Terminal 2 — Frontend:**
```bash
cd lament && bun run dev
```

Ensure the frontend's `.env` file points to the local API URL.
